    "result_text": "All 23 tests pass. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a **derived, seed-independent** field, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `membershipNumber` depends only on the owner's *own* fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`) and requires no repository state, I followed the codebase's existing pattern for such derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than adding a persisted column and pipeline step:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a null-safe default method that returns `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (using `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", ...)` so `YY` is zero-padded, e.g. year 2007 \u2192 `07`).\n\nThe method returns `null` when `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent, so seeded owners (whose rows populate neither column) don't break existing GET/list tests with an NPE. The derived approach also means the value survives the POST\u2192GET round trip the `Cp14Tests` exercises without needing a new column. Full suite: **23/23 green.**",
